# Classic Chocolate Chip Cookie Bars

Based on [Sally’s Baking Addiction](https://sallysbakingaddiction.com/soft-chewy-chocolate-chip-cookie-bars/)

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 2.25 cups (281g) [all-purpose flour]{ ing="all-purpose-flour" } (spooned & leveled)
- [ ] 1 tsp [baking soda]{ ing="baking-soda" }
- [ ] 1.5 tsp [cornstarch]{ ing="cornstarch" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 3/4 cup (12 Tbsp; 170g) [unsalted butter]{ ing="unsalted-butter" }, melted and slightly cooled
- [ ] 1 cup (200g) [packed light brown sugar]{ ing="packed-light-brown-sugar" }
- [ ] 1/3 cup (67g) [granulated sugar]{ ing="granulated-sugar" }
- [ ] 1 large egg plus 1 large [egg yolk]{ ing="egg-yolk" }, at room temperature
- [ ] 2 tsp [pure vanilla extract]{ ing="pure-vanilla-extract" }
- [ ] 1 cup (180g) [semi-sweet chocolate chips]{ ing="semi-sweet-chocolate-chips" }
- [ ] Optional: sprinkle of [flaky sea salt]{ ing="flaky-sea-salt" }

## Recipe

1. Preheat oven to 350°F (177°C). Line a 9-inch square baking pan with parchment paper, leaving excess paper around sides for easy removal.
1. In a large bowl, whisk together [flour]{ ing="all-purpose-flour" }, [baking soda]{ ing="baking-soda" }, [cornstarch]{ ing="cornstarch" }, and [salt]{ ing="salt" }. Set aside.
1. In a medium bowl, whisk melted [butter]{ ing="unsalted-butter" } with both [sugars]{ ing="packed-light-brown-sugar" } until lumps disappear. Add egg, [egg yolk]{ ing="egg-yolk" }, and vanilla. Pour wet ingredients into dry mixture and combine. Fold in [chocolate chips]{ ing="semi-sweet-chocolate-chips" }.
1. Transfer dough to prepared pan and press evenly. Optionally sprinkle [flaky sea salt]{ ing="flaky-sea-salt" } and additional [chocolate chips]{ ing="semi-sweet-chocolate-chips" } on top.
1. Bake 30-34 minutes until lightly browned on sides. Err on the side of under-baking and do not over-bake, or the cookie bars will taste a little dry and cakey.
1. Cool in pan for at least one hour, then lift out using parchment and cut into squares.

## Notes

- Store covered at room temperature up to one week.
